---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import UpdatedBadge from '../../components/content/UpdatedBadge.astro';
import ToolHero from '../../components/tools/ToolHero.astro';
import ToolHowItWorks from '../../components/tools/ToolHowItWorks.astro';
import ToolFAQ from '../../components/tools/ToolFAQ.astro';

const today = '2026-06-13T00:00:00+00:00';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is the Best Answer Hub QR Code Generator?',
    a: 'The Best Answer Hub QR Code Generator is a free browser-based tool that creates scannable QR codes from URLs, text, phone numbers, email addresses, and Wi-Fi credentials. Everything runs locally in your browser. No data is sent to any server. You can customize the size, colors, and error correction level, then download the QR code as a PNG image.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is the QR Code Generator free to use?',
    a: 'Yes, the Best Answer Hub QR Code Generator is completely free with no usage limits, no watermarks, and no signup required. You can create as many QR codes as you want, at any size, with full color customization. Unlike many competitors (such as QR Tiger and Beaconstac), the Best Answer Hub QR Code Generator does not cap the number of static codes or require an account.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What types of data can I encode in a QR code?',
    a: 'You can encode URLs, plain text, phone numbers, SMS messages, email addresses with subject and body, and Wi-Fi network credentials. Simply select the data type from the dropdown, fill in the fields, and the QR code updates instantly. For URLs, always include the full address starting with https:// for best compatibility.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the difference between static and dynamic QR codes?',
    a: 'Static QR codes encode data directly into the pattern itself. Once created, the data cannot be changed. Dynamic QR codes store a short redirect URL that points to your actual content, allowing you to change the destination later. The Best Answer Hub QR Code Generator creates static QR codes only. For dynamic codes, you need a paid service like Bitly, QR Tiger, or Flowcode that provides redirect hosting and analytics.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What QR code size should I use?',
    a: 'For digital use on websites and social media, 300 to 500 pixels is ideal. For print materials like business cards, use at least 500 pixels to ensure clean edges. For posters and signage, 800 to 1000 pixels works best. The general rule is that the QR code should be at least 2 x 2 centimeters when printed for reliable scanning from a normal distance.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is error correction and which level should I choose?',
    a: 'Error correction allows a QR code to still scan even if part of it is damaged, dirty, or covered. Low (L) recovers 7% of data, Medium (M) recovers 15%, Quartile (Q) recovers 25%, and High (H) recovers 30%. For most purposes, Medium (M) is the best balance. Choose High (H) if you plan to add a logo in the center or expect the code to be exposed to wear and tear.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I customize the colors of my QR code?',
    a: 'Yes. You can change the foreground color (the dark modules) and the background color. However, for reliable scanning, always maintain strong contrast between the two colors. Black on white works best. Avoid light-on-light combinations like yellow on white or pastel on pastel, as most phone cameras struggle to read them.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will my QR code work with any phone or scanner?',
    a: 'Yes. The QR codes generated by the Best Answer Hub QR Code Generator follow the international ISO 18004 standard, which means they work with any modern smartphone camera app, including iPhone Camera, Google Lens, Samsung Camera, and dedicated QR scanner apps on Android and iOS. Older phones without built-in QR scanning may need a third-party scanner app.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I add a logo or image to the center of my QR code?',
    a: 'No, the Best Answer Hub QR Code Generator does not support logo embedding. Adding a logo requires advanced image processing to maintain the error correction data. If you need branded QR codes with your logo in the center, use a paid service like QR Tiger, Beaconstac, or Adobe Express. When using such tools, always set error correction to High (H) to compensate for the logo covering part of the pattern.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long do QR codes last?',
    a: 'Static QR codes last forever because the data is embedded directly in the pattern. There is no server, no subscription, and no expiration date. As long as the printed or digital image remains scannable, the QR code will work. Dynamic QR codes, by contrast, only work as long as the redirect service hosting them remains active and paid.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the maximum amount of text a QR code can hold?',
    a: 'A standard QR code can hold up to 4,296 alphanumeric characters, 7,089 numeric characters, or 2,953 bytes of binary data. For URLs, this is rarely a concern since most web addresses are under 100 characters. For plain text, very long passages may require a higher resolution image or may fail to scan reliably. Keep URLs short for best results.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I track how many people scan my QR code?',
    a: 'No. The Best Answer Hub QR Code Generator creates static QR codes, which means there is no server involved and no way to track scans. If you need scan analytics (such as location, time, device type, or total scans), you need a dynamic QR code service like Bitly, QR Tiger, or Scanova. These services redirect through their servers, allowing them to collect usage data.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why is my QR code not scanning?',
    a: 'The most common reasons are low contrast between foreground and background colors, a code that is too small or blurry, inverted colors (white on black instead of black on white), or too much data crammed into a small image. To fix it, increase the size, switch to black on white, reduce the amount of text, or increase the error correction level to High.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the best free QR code generator?',
    a: 'The best free QR code generator depends on your needs. For simple, no-signup creation with full privacy, browser-based tools are ideal because nothing is uploaded to a server. For dynamic codes with analytics, Bitly and QR Tiger offer free tiers with limited scans. For branded codes with logos, Adobe Express and Canva provide free design tools. For maximum privacy and unlimited static codes, a client-side generator like the Best Answer Hub QR Code Generator is the best choice.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is it safe to scan a QR code? What is quishing?',
    a: 'Scanning a QR code itself does not install malware or expose your device. The risk is always in where the code points. QR code phishing (called quishing) is a fast-growing attack where criminals create codes that direct victims to fake bank login pages, credential-harvesting sites, or malware downloads. Quishing attacks surged 146% in Q1 2026 according to Microsoft threat intelligence data, making it one of the fastest-growing cyber threats on record. To stay safe: only scan QR codes from sources you trust, always check the URL preview your phone shows before tapping "open", and be alert to codes stuck over existing ones on ATMs, parking meters, or restaurant tables. QR codes generated by the Best Answer Hub QR Code Generator are static codes that encode exactly the data you enter: the security responsibility is always in the destination URL, not the code format itself.',
  },
];

const steps = [
  { title: 'Choose data type', description: 'Select what you want to encode: a URL, text, phone number, email, SMS, or Wi-Fi credentials. Each type has its own input fields.' },
  { title: 'Enter your data', description: 'Fill in the details. For URLs, include the full https:// address. The QR code preview updates instantly as you type.' },
  { title: 'Customize and download', description: 'Adjust the size, colors, and error correction level. Then download your QR code as a PNG image ready for print or digital use.' },
];

const seo = {
  title: 'Free QR Code Generator — Scannable QR Codes (2026)',
  description: 'Create free QR codes for URLs, text, phone, email, and Wi-Fi. No signup. No watermarks. Customize size, colors, and error correction. Download PNG instantly.',
  url: '/tools/qr-code-generator/',
  type: 'WebPage' as const,
  datePublished: today,
  dateModified: today,
  breadcrumbs: [
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Tools', url: '/tools/' },
    { name: 'QR Code Generator', url: '/tools/qr-code-generator/' },
  ],
  faq: faqs.map(f => ({ question: f.q, answer: f.a.replace(/<[^>]*>/g, '').replace(/\s{2,}/g, ' ').trim() })),
};
---

<BaseLayout seo={seo}>
  <ToolHero
    badge="Free Tool · No Upload to Servers"
    title="QR Code Generator:"
    accentText="Create scannable codes instantly"
    description="Generate QR codes for URLs, text, phone numbers, emails, and Wi-Fi. Fully customizable size, colors, and error correction. No watermarks, no signup. Download PNG in seconds."
    backLink="/tools/"
    backLabel="← All Tools"
  />

  <!-- Generator Interface -->
  <section class="py-6 md:py-8" aria-label="QR code generator">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="mb-5"><UpdatedBadge date={seo.dateModified} /></div>
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-5 gap-6">
          <!-- Controls -->
          <div class="md:col-span-3 bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6 space-y-5">
            <!-- Data Type -->
            <div>
              <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Data type</label>
              <select id="qr-type" class="w-full bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-bae-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-bae-primary/30 focus:border-bae-primary">
                <option value="url">URL (Website link)</option>
                <option value="text">Plain text</option>
                <option value="phone">Phone number</option>
                <option value="sms">SMS message</option>
                <option value="email">Email address</option>
                <option value="wifi">Wi-Fi network</option>
              </select>
            </div>

            <!-- URL Input -->
            <div id="input-url">
              <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Website URL</label>
              <input type="url" id="qr-url" placeholder="https://example.com" class="w-full bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-bae-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-bae-primary/30 focus:border-bae-primary" />
            </div>

            <!-- Text Input -->
            <div id="input-text" class="hidden">
              <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Text content</label>
              <textarea id="qr-text" rows="3" placeholder="Enter any text..." class="w-full bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-bae-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-bae-primary/30 focus:border-bae-primary resize-y"></textarea>
            </div>

            <!-- Phone Input -->
            <div id="input-phone" class="hidden">
              <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Phone number</label>
              <input type="tel" id="qr-phone" placeholder="+1 234 567 8900" class="w-full bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-bae-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-bae-primary/30 focus:border-bae-primary" />
            </div>

            <!-- SMS Input -->
            <div id="input-sms" class="hidden space-y-3">
              <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Phone number</label>
                <input type="tel" id="qr-sms-phone" placeholder="+1 234 567 8900" class="w-full bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-bae-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-bae-primary/30 focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>
              <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Message</label>
                <textarea id="qr-sms-body" rows="2" placeholder="Your message..." class="w-full bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-bae-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-bae-primary/30 focus:border-bae-primary resize-y"></textarea>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Email Input -->
            <div id="input-email" class="hidden space-y-3">
              <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Email address</label>
                <input type="email" id="qr-email-addr" placeholder="hello@example.com" class="w-full bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-bae-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-bae-primary/30 focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>
              <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Subject</label>
                <input type="text" id="qr-email-subj" placeholder="Email subject" class="w-full bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-bae-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-bae-primary/30 focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>
              <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Body</label>
                <textarea id="qr-email-body" rows="2" placeholder="Email body..." class="w-full bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-bae-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-bae-primary/30 focus:border-bae-primary resize-y"></textarea>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Wi-Fi Input -->
            <div id="input-wifi" class="hidden space-y-3">
              <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Network name (SSID)</label>
                <input type="text" id="qr-wifi-ssid" placeholder="MyWiFi" class="w-full bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-bae-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-bae-primary/30 focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>
              <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Password</label>
                <input type="text" id="qr-wifi-pass" placeholder="WiFi password" class="w-full bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-bae-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-bae-primary/30 focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>
              <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Encryption</label>
                <select id="qr-wifi-enc" class="w-full bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-bae-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-bae-primary/30 focus:border-bae-primary">
                  <option value="WPA">WPA/WPA2</option>
                  <option value="WEP">WEP</option>
                  <option value="nopass">None / Open</option>
                </select>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Size -->
            <div>
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                <label class="text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink">Size</label>
                <span id="size-value" class="text-xs text-bae-muted font-mono">300 px</span>
              </div>
              <input type="range" id="qr-size" min="100" max="1000" value="300" step="50" class="w-full accent-bae-primary h-1.5 bg-bae-border rounded-lg appearance-none cursor-pointer" />
              <div class="flex justify-between text-[10px] text-bae-muted mt-1">
                <span>100px</span>
                <span>1000px</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Error Correction -->
            <div>
              <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Error correction</label>
              <div class="grid grid-cols-4 gap-2">
                <button type="button" data-ec="1" class="ec-btn px-2 py-2 text-xs font-medium rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-bae-bg text-bae-muted hover:text-bae-ink transition-colors">Low</button>
                <button type="button" data-ec="0" class="ec-btn px-2 py-2 text-xs font-medium rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-primary bg-bae-primary text-white transition-colors">Medium</button>
                <button type="button" data-ec="3" class="ec-btn px-2 py-2 text-xs font-medium rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-bae-bg text-bae-muted hover:text-bae-ink transition-colors">Quartile</button>
                <button type="button" data-ec="2" class="ec-btn px-2 py-2 text-xs font-medium rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-bae-bg text-bae-muted hover:text-bae-ink transition-colors">High</button>
              </div>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-bae-muted mt-1.5">Medium balances scan reliability and data density.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Colors -->
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Foreground</label>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                  <input type="color" id="qr-fg" value="#000000" class="w-8 h-8 rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border cursor-pointer bg-transparent" />
                  <span id="qr-fg-val" class="text-xs text-bae-muted font-mono">#000000</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Background</label>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                  <input type="color" id="qr-bg" value="#ffffff" class="w-8 h-8 rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border cursor-pointer bg-transparent" />
                  <span id="qr-bg-val" class="text-xs text-bae-muted font-mono">#ffffff</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Preview -->
          <div class="md:col-span-2">
            <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6 sticky top-24">
              <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink mb-4">Preview</h3>
              <div class="bg-white rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border p-6 flex items-center justify-center min-h-[240px]">
                <div id="qr-preview"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="mt-4 space-y-2">
                <a id="qr-download" href="#" download="qrcode.png" class="block w-full text-center bg-bae-primary text-white font-semibold text-sm py-2.5 rounded-bae-sm hover:bg-bae-accent transition-colors no-underline">
                  Download PNG
                </a>
                <button type="button" id="qr-clear" class="block w-full text-center bg-bae-bg text-bae-muted border border-bae-border font-semibold text-sm py-2.5 rounded-bae-sm hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors">
                  Clear
                </button>
                <p class="text-[11px] text-bae-muted text-center">Scan with your phone camera to test</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Limitations -->
  <section class="py-6 md:py-8 border-t border-bae-border-light">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-bae p-4 md:p-5">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-amber-600 shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-2.5L13.732 4c-.77-.833-1.964-.833-2.732 0L4.082 16.5c-.77.833.192 2.5 1.732 2.5z"/></svg>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-2">What this tool cannot do</h3>
            <ul class="text-sm text-amber-700 space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside">
              <li><strong>Dynamic QR codes:</strong> These QR codes are static. The data cannot be changed after creation. For editable or trackable codes, use a paid service like QR Tiger or Bitly.</li>
              <li><strong>Logo embedding:</strong> Adding a logo in the center requires advanced processing. Use QR Tiger, Beaconstac, or Adobe Express for branded codes.</li>
              <li><strong>Scan analytics:</strong> There is no server involved, so scan counts, locations, or device data cannot be tracked.</li>
              <li><strong>Low contrast colors:</strong> Pastel-on-pastel or light-on-light color combinations may not scan reliably. Stick to high-contrast pairs.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ToolHowItWorks steps={steps} />

  <!-- QR Code Use Cases -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-[1.75rem] font-bold text-bae-ink mb-2">Popular use cases</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted mb-6">How people and businesses use QR codes</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft flex items-center justify-center text-bae-primary text-sm font-bold mb-3">1</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">Business cards</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Link directly to your LinkedIn profile, portfolio, or contact page so people can connect without typing a long URL.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft flex items-center justify-center text-bae-primary text-sm font-bold mb-3">2</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">Restaurant menus</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Place a QR code on tables linking to an online menu. Update the menu page anytime without reprinting the codes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft flex items-center justify-center text-bae-primary text-sm font-bold mb-3">3</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">Wi-Fi sharing</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Guests scan once to connect. No need to read out long passwords or type them character by character.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft flex items-center justify-center text-bae-primary text-sm font-bold mb-3">4</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">Event check-in</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Send QR codes in email invitations. Attendees scan at the door for instant check-in without printed tickets.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft flex items-center justify-center text-bae-primary text-sm font-bold mb-3">5</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">Product packaging</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Link to instruction manuals, warranty registration, or tutorial videos, reducing paper waste and support calls.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft flex items-center justify-center text-bae-primary text-sm font-bold mb-3">6</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">Feedback forms</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Print QR codes on receipts or invoices linking to Google Forms, Typeform, or SurveyMonkey for instant reviews.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ToolFAQ faqs={faqs} />

  <!-- Who uses this tool -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-[1.75rem] font-bold text-bae-ink mb-8">Who reaches for this tool</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">RESTAURANT OWNER</div>
          <div class="text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-1">The Restaurant Owner</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-primary font-serif mb-2">MENU UPDATED INSTANTLY</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Switching from paper menus to a digital menu page, they generate a QR code pointing to their Google Drive PDF or website menu. Printed on a table tent at 500px, customers can scan without touching anything, and the owner updates the menu without reprinting.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">FREELANCE CONSULTANT</div>
          <div class="text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-1">The Freelance Consultant</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-primary font-serif mb-2">NETWORKING MADE EASY</div>
